{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>לצנאכם.</b> This word is derived from ״צֹנֶה וַאֲלָפִים כֻּלָּם״ (Psalms 8) — which has no alef intervening between the nun and the tsadi, and the alef that appears here after the nun stands in place of the heh of צֹנֶה. This I learned from the method of R. Moshe HaDarshan." "<b>And what proceeds from your mouth you shall do.</b> In excess — for they took upon themselves to cross over for the war until conquest and division, since Moshe asked of them only ״וְנִכְבְּשָׁה … וְאַחַר תָּשׁוּבוּ״, but they took upon themselves ״עַד הִתְנַחֵל״ — behold, they added to delay seven years during which the land was divided, and so they did."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:35.681360268Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}